        "contenuto_esteso": "12 Updates Auto-updates live-orange 5m ago ( 07:55 GMT ) Operations temporarily suspended at Abu Dhabi’s Habshan gas complex Operations at the Habshan gas complex have been temporarily suspended the Abu Dhabi media has office said. In a statement on X, the media office said that local authorities have confirmed that the fire was caused by falling debris following a missile interception by Abu Dhabi’s air defence systems. The interception also injured two Emiratis and one Indian national, the media office added. live-orange 10m ago ( 07:50 GMT ) Hezbollah abides by ceasefire Hezbollah has accepted the two-week ceasefire despite Israel’s continued attacks on Lebanon, three Lebanese sources close to the group told Reuters news agency The group halted fire on northern Israel and on Israeli troops in Lebanon in the early hours of Wednesday as part of the US-Iran ceasefire. Israel has continued its strikes on southern Lebanon and issued a new evacuation order for one southern city, indicating it would strike there soon, after Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said the two-week Iran-US ceasefire would not include Lebanon. live-orange 10m ago ( 07:50 GMT ) France says ceasefire deal should include Lebanon French President Emmanuel Macron has welcomed the ceasefire between the US and Iran and said, “It is a very good thing.” Macron, however, warned that the situation in Lebanon is critical and said the ceasefire deal should include Lebanon. Advertisement live-orange 15m ago ( 07:45 GMT ) Iran’s Ghalibaf, US’s Vance expected at Islamabad talks on Friday Parliament Speaker Mohammad Bagher Ghalibaf is set to lead Iran’s negotiating team in Friday’s talks in Pakistan’s capital Islamabad, which is expected to see Vice President JD Vance represent the US delegation, according to Iran’s ISNA news agency. The report said Iran’s 10-point proposal framework includes not only its nuclear programme and regional security, but also Iran’s primary and secondary sanctions, which date back about 45 years. live-orange 20m ago ( 07:40 GMT ) Humanity came ‘perilously close to disaster’, Spain’s foreign minister says after ceasefire Spain’s Foreign Minister Jose Manuel Albares has said that the world came “perilously close” to disaster after US President Donald Trump threatened to wipe out Iranian civilisation in his ultimatum to Tehran. Following the announcement of a ceasefire, Albares told RNE radio station that Trump’s ultimatum [to Iran] was “absolutely unacceptable for humankind” and it was too early to determine whether the conflict was definitively over. “When the leader of a military superpower makes such threats, I take them seriously,” he added. live-orange 30m ago ( 07:30 GMT ) In Strait of Hormuz, Iran and China take aim at US dollar hegemony By John Power As the United States-Israel war on Iran – paused for two weeks on Wednesday amid new diplomatic talks – has roiled the global economy for more than a month, Iran and China have seized the opportunity to address a shared gripe about the global financial system. Their common cause: Ending the hegemony of the US dollar. For years, they say, Washington has leveraged the dominance of the dollar in international trade to exert influence and inflict pain on enemies and competitors, Iran and China included. The supremacy of the dollar is especially apparent in the global oil market, where about 80 percent of transactions are settled in the currency, according to a 2023 estimate by JPMorgan Chase. Read the full story here . live-orange 35m ago ( 07:25 GMT ) Lebanon’s army advises citizens to avoid south of the country Lebanon’s Army has called on citizens returning to villages and towns in the south of the country to avoid approaching areas infiltrated by Israel. “In light of the regional developments and the circulation of reports about a ceasefire, the army command calls on citizens to refrain from returning to the southern villages and towns and to avoid approaching areas where Israeli forces have advanced, in order to preserve their safety, especially as they may expose their lives to the danger of ongoing Israeli attacks,” the army said in a statement. Israel has said the ceasefire between the US and Iran will not include Lebanon and issued a new forced evacuation threat for one southern city early today, indicating it would strike there soon. The Lebanese army also advised residents in the south to adhere to the directives of Lebanon’s deployed military units and to exercise utmost caution and vigilance with respect to any unexploded ordnance and suspicious objects found in the region. live-orange 40m ago ( 07:20 GMT ) US-Israel suffered ‘crushing defeat’ in Iran, Russia’s Foreign Ministry says Maria Zakharova, Russia’s Foreign Ministry spokeswoman, says the United States and Israel launched “a one-track aggressive unprovoked attack” on Iran on February 28, which led to a “crushing defeat”. “Our country, from the very beginning, in its first statements, said that it was necessary to immediately stop this aggression, that there was no military solution to this situation or any attempt to establish order in the region,” she said on Sputnik radio. Zakharova also said it was necessary to immediately begin “a real political and diplomatic settlement, which, of course, is based on the negotiation process with a real consideration of positions”. live-orange 50m ago ( 07:10 GMT ) Two Palestinians killed in separate shooting incidents in Israel Two Palestinians, including a teenager, were shot and killed in separate incidents in two mixed-Arab cities in Israel, according to the Palestinian news agency Wafa. According to Wafa, Mustafa Ahmad Shaaban, 42, and Yazan Masarwa, 15, were killed in separate shooting incidents in the cities of Lod and Kafr Qara on Tuesday night. Since the beginning of this year, at least 79 Palestinians have been killed within the Palestinian communities inside the 1948 territories, according to Wafa. Meanwhile, in the town of Nahf, a 23-year-old man was also “critically injured” after being shot. He is currently being treated at a hospital. Advertisement live-orange 55m ago ( 07:05 GMT ) How many people have been killed? live-orange 57m ago ( 07:03 GMT ) If you’re just joining us Let’s bring you up to speed: US President Donald Trump announced a last-minute deal with Iran , paving the way for a two-week cessation of US-Israeli hostilities and a temporary reopening of the Strait of Hormuz. Spontaneous celebration erupted in Tehran as Iran declared it had forced Trump to accept its 10-point demand for a truce, which would include the safe passage of ships through the Strait of Hormuz in coordination with the Iranian armed forces. Pakistan’s Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif, who mediated the deal, says the agreement between Iran and the US also includes “Lebanon and elsewhere”. Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said he supports Trump’s ceasefire announcement, but said the deal does not cover Lebanon. Dozens of Democratic lawmakers condemned Trump’s threatening rhetoric towards Iran and called for his removal from office. Oman’s Foreign Ministry welcomed the announcement of a ceasefire, but other Gulf countries are reporting ongoing attacks from Iran. live-orange 1h ago ( 07:00 GMT ) Welcome to our coverage Hello and welcome to our live coverage of the war between the United States, Israel and Iran. Stay with us for the latest developments, reactions and analysis from across the Middle East and beyond. You can find our updates from Tuesday, April 7 here ."
